SUMMARY:Attachment can hide
DESCRIPTION:John of the Cross\n\nIDEA\nEven attachment to good experiences can narrow perception when the experience becomes an end in itself.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: G. K. Chesterton\, “Test wonder.” That thought was working with wonder\; today’s works with detachment. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nAscent of Mount Carmel. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
