DESCRIPTION:Søren Kierkegaard\n\nIDEA\nExistential commitment begins where detached calculation can no longer make the decision for you.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: John Cage\, “Attention alters noise.” That thought was working with attention\; today’s works with choice. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nFear and Trembling / Concluding Unscientific Postscript. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
