DESCRIPTION:Christopher Alexander\n\nIDEA\nA good local change improves not only its target but the larger field of relationships around it.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Søren Kierkegaard\, “Can certainty choose?.” That thought was working with choice\; today’s works with pattern. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nA Pattern Language / The Nature of Order. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
