SUMMARY:Test hope
DESCRIPTION:Jürgen Moltmann\n\nIDEA\nHope is not confidence that present trends will turn out well. It can oppose the apparent finality of the present by orienting life toward what is promised but not yet actual.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Marshall McLuhan\, “Test medium.” That thought was working with media\; today’s works with hope. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nTheology of Hope. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
