DESCRIPTION:Gregory of Nyssa\n\nIDEA\nFulfillment need not extinguish desire. Encounter can enlarge the capacity for further encounter.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Dante Gabriel Rossetti\, “Invert past.” That thought was working with imagination\; today’s works with desire. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nLife of Moses. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
