DESCRIPTION:Nicholas of Cusa\n\nIDEA\nFinite measures cannot simply be extrapolated until they become adequate to the infinite.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Carl Jung\, “Invert projection.” That thought was working with self\; today’s works with scale. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nOn Learned Ignorance. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
