DESCRIPTION:Ivan Illich\n\nIDEA\nInstitutions can manufacture dependence by redefining ordinary capacities as deficiencies requiring professional supply.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nIvan Illich appeared within the previous seven days with “Help can disable.” Both thoughts touch tools\, but the overlap was accidental. Read them together without assuming agreement: does Ivan Illich deepen the earlier thought\, contradict its emphasis\, or reveal that the shared vocabulary conceals different projects?\n\nCONTEXT\nsocial criticism. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
