SUMMARY:Invert image
DESCRIPTION:Dante Gabriel Rossetti\n\nIDEA\nWhen image and poem address the same subject\, neither need merely illustrate the other\; each can alter how the other is read.\n\nINVERT\nReverse the usual priority for a moment. What becomes newly visible?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Carl Jung\, “Invert projection.” That thought was working with self\; today’s works with image. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\ndouble works / sonnet-painting relations. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
