DESCRIPTION:Carl Jung\n\nIDEA\nWhat appears to belong entirely to another person may partly reveal material the observer has not recognized as their own.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Ivan Illich\, “Invert help.” That thought was working with tools\; today’s works with self. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nprojection. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
