SUMMARY:Test restlessness
DESCRIPTION:Augustine of Hippo\n\nIDEA\nRestlessness is not only a defect to suppress\; it can reveal that a desire has mistaken a finite object for its final home.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Julian of Norwich\, “Test smallness.” That thought was working with scale\; today’s works with desire. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nConfessions. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
