DESCRIPTION:Eugen Fink\n\nIDEA\nPlay is not merely an escape from reality. It can disclose a distinctive world with its own seriousness\, rules\, and horizon.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Teresa of Ávila\, “Prayer can be practical.” That thought was working with practice\; today’s works with play. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nPlay as Symbol of the World. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
