SUMMARY:Invert future
DESCRIPTION:Jürgen Moltmann\n\nIDEA\nThe future is not only what comes later. Anticipated possibility can interrupt the present and alter what counts as realistic.\n\nINVERT\nReverse the usual priority for a moment. What becomes newly visible?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Syncletica of Alexandria\, “Invert burden.” That thought was working with practice\; today’s works with hope. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nTheology of Hope. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
