SUMMARY:Name the thought-pattern
DESCRIPTION:Evagrius Ponticus\n\nIDEA\nSeeing a thought as a recurring kind of event can loosen its claim to be simply identical with reality.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: John of the Cross\, “Absence refines desire.” That thought was working with desire\; today’s works with attention. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nPraktikos. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
