SUMMARY:Test fire
DESCRIPTION:Macarius of Egypt\n\nIDEA\nTransformation is often described not as external correction but as an interior change in what the person can perceive and desire.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Pseudo-Dionysius\, “Invert excess.” That thought was working with unknowing\; today’s works with transformation. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nMacarian Homilies. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
