SUMMARY:Restlessness can guide
DESCRIPTION:Augustine of Hippo\n\nIDEA\nRestlessness is not only a defect to suppress\; it can reveal that a desire has mistaken a finite object for its final home.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: William Blake\, “Test contraries.” That thought was working with paradox\; today’s works with desire. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nConfessions. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
