SUMMARY:Test making
DESCRIPTION:Jacques Maritain\n\nIDEA\nArtistic intelligence can know its object through disciplined making rather than detached inspection alone.\n\nTEST\nWhere does this idea fail\, and what does that failure reveal about its proper scope?\n\nCONVERSATION\nGeorge Herbert appeared within the previous seven days with “Test enactment.” Both thoughts touch making\, but the overlap was accidental. Read them together without assuming agreement: does Jacques Maritain deepen the earlier thought\, contradict its emphasis\, or reveal that the shared vocabulary conceals different projects?\n\nCONTEXT\nCreative Intuition in Art and Poetry. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
