SUMMARY:Invert paradox
DESCRIPTION:G. K. Chesterton\n\nIDEA\nA paradox can expose an assumption so familiar that ordinary formulation leaves it invisible.\n\nINVERT\nReverse the usual priority for a moment. What becomes newly visible?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Ivan Illich\, “Test limits.” That thought was working with tools\; today’s works with paradox. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nessays and apologetics. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
