SUMMARY:Invert infinite
DESCRIPTION:Nicholas of Cusa\n\nIDEA\nFinite measures cannot simply be extrapolated until they become adequate to the infinite.\n\nINVERT\nReverse the usual priority for a moment. What becomes newly visible?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Augustine of Hippo\, “Restlessness can guide.” That thought was working with desire\; today’s works with scale. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nOn Learned Ignorance. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
