DESCRIPTION:Teresa of Ávila\n\nIDEA\nDifferent modes of awareness can coexist within one person without all being equally accessible at once.\n\nNOTICE\nWhat becomes visible if you treat this as a claim about perception rather than as a slogan?\n\nCONVERSATION\nAn accidental neighbor from the previous seven days: Christopher Alexander\, “Test repair.” That thought was working with pattern\; today’s works with self. Put them beside each other and ask whether one changes the scale\, frame\, or stakes of the other. If the connection does not survive attention\, let it fail rather than manufacturing one.\n\nCONTEXT\nInterior Castle. This entry is a compact conceptual paraphrase\, not a quotation.
